oms experience: a concept analysis</article-title><source>Oncol Nurs Forum</source><year>2003</year><volume>30</volume><fpage>601</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12861321</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b22-co15-5-211"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Walsh</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Rybicki</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Symptom clustering in advanced cancer</article-title><source>Support Care Cancer</source><year>2006</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>831</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16482450</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b23-co15-5-211"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name><name><surname>Tseng</surname><given-names>HC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Symptom clusters in cancer patients</article-title><source>Support Care Cancer</source><year>2006</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>825</fpage><lpage>30</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16491377</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b24-co15-5-211"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Okuyama</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>XS</given-names></name><name><surname>Akechi</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Japanese version of the MD Anderson Symptom Inventory: a validation study</article-title><source>J Pain Symptom Manage</source><year>2003</year><volume>26</volume><fpage>1093</fpage><lpage>104</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14654261</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-wrap><fig id="f1-co15-5-211" position="float"><label>FIGURE 1</label><caption><p>Biplot between components 1 and 2.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="c